---
title: "Row Pinning"
---

Pinned rows appear either above or below the normal rows of a table.
This feature in other grids is also known as **Frozen Rows** or **Floating Rows**.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Simple Row Pinning" name="simple-pinning"  exampleHeight=580 /%}

There are two ways to achieve row pinning in the grid. They are described in their own sections:

- [Static Pinned Rows](./row-pinning-static)
- [Manually Pinned Rows](./row-pinning-manual)

## Next Update

Continue to the next section to learn about [Static Pinned Rows](./row-pinning-static)
